Template: geant4/datasets
Type: multiselect
Choices: @CHOICES@
Default: @DEFAULTS@
Description: Geant4 data files to download:
 Geant4 needs data files that are distributed separately, and they are
 downloaded from cern.ch while this package installs rather than carried
 inside it.
 .
 All of them are selected by default.  Seven are required -- Geant4 treats
 them as fatal when missing and nothing runs without them: G4EMLOW,
 PhotonEvaporation, RadioactiveDecay, G4PARTICLEXS, G4ABLA, G4INCL and
 G4ENSDFSTATE.  The other five are needed only for specific physics --
 neutron transport with the _hp physics lists, PIXE, optical surfaces, the
 SAID cross-sections and crystal channelling -- and account for about 1.3 GB
 of the 1.65 GB download.
 .
 Selecting none is allowed; the datasets can be added later with
 @PREFIX@/share/Geant4/fetch-datasets.sh.

Template: geant4/download-failed
Type: note
Description: Some Geant4 data files could not be downloaded
 One or more datasets failed to download or did not match their checksum.
 Geant4 itself is installed and the other datasets are in place, but the
 missing ones have to be fetched before the corresponding physics will work.
 .
 To retry, once the network allows it:
 .
  sudo @PREFIX@/share/Geant4/fetch-datasets.sh
